      "agu:justification": [
        {
          "@type": "CreativeWork",
          "agu:sequence": 1,
          "text": "There are many reasons why IMERG is uniquely useful and impactful. First and foremost it is because it is a global dataset describing with high temporal and spatial resolution precipitation. Precipitation is a critical component of the water cycle, and it has a direct connection to society, the environment and natural hazards. The urgency to make progress in this field is evident as the availability and access to freshwater is at risk in many parts of the world, and floods and droughts become more frequent and more severe. Accordingly, the United Nations (UN) has declared an “International Decade for Action on Water for Sustainable Development” (2018-2028; https://www.un.org/en/events/waterdecade). The facts and figures are frightening and demonstrate a clear need to better understand, document and predict the hydrological cycle including the precipitation component: • 2.1 billion…"
        },
        {
          "@type": "CreativeWork",
          "agu:sequence": 2,
          "text": "IMERG is a multi-sensor precipitation data of global coverage at high frequency (hourly) and resolution (km scale). It represents a crowning jewel achievement of decades of satellite based precipitation estimation as a community (that culminated in the Global Precipitation Mission) with a convergence and confluence of tested methods to yield a usable precipitation product that is also accessible for research and societal applications. As a user and researcher of water resources to solve water-related problems, IMERG more than a product. It has facilitated numerous stories of hope for farmers from the Indus to the Bengal delta and farther (to the Mekong). It has allowed efficient irrigation for these farmers, efficient monitoring of reservoirs for many countries for better planning and reservoir operations strategy"
        },
        {
          "@type": "CreativeWork",
          "agu:sequence": 3,
          "text": "The IMERG dataset has fundamentally changed how we understand and are able to respond to precipitation events around the world. It feels critical to identify gaps in regions where other satellite-derived data, and especially surface weather observations, are sparse. What makes IMERG so impactful isn't just that it provides precipitation data - it's that it provides globally consistent, high-quality precipitation data to places and applications that never had it before. IMERG can be used for global-scale applications and is especially useful over regions with sparse or no reliable surface observations. The fine spatial and temporal resolution of IMERG data allows them to be accumulated to the scale of the application for increased skill. It is well recognized that long-term precipitation measurements are necessary for understanding and monitoring regional precipitation characteristics.…"
        },
        {
          "@type": "CreativeWork",
          "agu:sequence": 4,
          "text": "The IMERG dataset is a highly valuable tool for environmental monitoring, hydraulic design of infrastructure, and disaster risk management. Reliable precipitation data is important for developing meteorological, hydrological, and water management applications. Being able to estimate rainfall with enough accuracy also helps to describe and anticipate physical processes at different spatial scales, such as floods, landslides, soil erosion, and severe storms. Rain gauge measurements, however, are still limited in number and unevenly distributed around the world. Satellite-based precipitation products offer a practical alternative. One advantage of satellite estimates is that they can be used in areas without rain gauges or weather radar coverage. They also help improve rainfall information in regions where gauges are available. In addition, they provide relatively consistent historical…"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "Dataset",
      "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:dataset:agu-0003",
      "mainEntityOfPage": "https://impactfuldatasets.agu.org/#/dataset/agu-0003",
