        }
      ],
      "agu:reuseExample": [
        {
          "@type": "CreativeWork",
          "text": "Argo Bibliography: https://argo.ucsd.edu/outreach/publications/bibliography/ Argo data products catalogued here: Argo data products | Argo and BGC: Biogeochemical Argo | Data Products Argo Data…"
        },
        {
          "@type": "CreativeWork",
          "text": "The Argo program maintains a bibliography demonstrating the remarkable impact of the data: https://argo.ucsd.edu/outreach/publications/bibliography/"
        }
      ],
      "agu:nominator": [
        {
          "@type": "Person",
          "@id": "https://orcid.org/0009-0006-5535-9362",
          "name": "A.J. Reiss",
          "affiliation": {
            "@type": "Organization",
            "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:organization:noaa-nws-ocean-prediction-center-5830-university-research-court-colleg",
            "name": "NOAA-NWS-Ocean Prediction Center, 5830 University Research Court, College Park, MD 20740"
          },
          "agu:sequence": 1
        },
        {
          "@type": "Person",
          "@id": "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9144-4368",
          "name": "Sarah Gille",
          "affiliation": {
            "@type": "Organization",
            "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:organization:scripps-institution-of-oceanography-ucsd-9500-gilman-dr-mail-code-0230",
            "name": "Scripps Institution of Oceanography, UCSD, 9500 Gilman Dr., Mail Code 0230, La Jolla, CA 92093-0230"
          },
          "agu:sequence": 2
        },
        {
          "@type": "Person",
          "@id": "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5100-4595",
          "name": "Catia M Domingues",
          "affiliation": {
            "@type": "Organization",
            "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:organization:global-climate-national-oceanography-centre-noc-waterfront-campus-euro",
            "name": "Global Climate, National Oceanography Centre (NOC), Waterfront Campus, European Way, Southampton, Hampshire, SO14 3ZH, UK"
          },
          "agu:sequence": 3
        }
      ],
      "agu:justification": [
        {
          "@type": "CreativeWork",
          "agu:sequence": 1,
          "text": "The Ocean Prediction Center is responsible for protecting life and property at sea and defending the resilience of our nation's global supply chains carrying on America's $360B+ worth of international maritime trade and fisheries. Their mission depends on their operational marine weather models that depend on forcing and energy exchange with the ocean. Argo is the most persistent, present, accurate and reliable oceanographic sensor measuring the key parameters in the ocean from the surface to a significant depth. The very ocean description that forces the atmosphere above it. Argo consistently and significantly drives more accuracy into their models which drives more accuracy into our life and property saving mission."
        },
        {
          "@type": "CreativeWork",
          "agu:sequence": 2,
          "text": "Since the start of the Argo program some 25 years ago, Argo has transformed understanding of the ocean and of changing properties of the ocean. Argo has demonstrated that most of the excess heat stored by the Earth system is contained in the top 2000 m of the ocean, enabling the closure of the Earth's energy budget and clarifying the relative roles of warming and ice melt in driving sea level rise. Every day, Argo provides near-real-time information about ocean temperature and salt, as well as biogeochemical variables, supplying critical information for ocean and atmospheric forecasting. Argo information has helped drive operational forecast improvements, and at the same time, it has provided reliable information to advance understanding of the mechanisms that drive ocean physics and chemistry. The Argo program is coordinated through a visionary international coordination effort that…"
        },
        {
          "@type": "CreativeWork",
          "agu:sequence": 3,
          "text": "Before Argo data, the scientific community’s view of the ocean interior resembled an old, incomplete map, biased toward ship routes and northern summers. Although it was well known that the ocean was central to Earth’s climate, only limited glimpses of its vast interior were available. Quantifying global change was an exercise in extrapolation. Forecasting was constrained by limited knowledge of the subsurface ocean, the hidden driver of weather, climate, ecosystems and biodiversity. The Argo dataset transformed this picture. With a global fleet of robotic profiling floats, the scientific community gained a continuous, all-season, subsurface view of the changing ocean for the first time over the past 25 years. It changed what can be observed, known, and done across all three AGU dimensions of impact. Planet – from inference to direct observation Argo enables more precise quantification…"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "Dataset",
      "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:dataset:agu-0005",
