      "name": "ARTMIP Database",
      "alternateName": "",
      "keywords": {
        "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:theme:atmos"
      },
      "agu:datasetId": "agu-0005",
      "agu:stableKey": "title:artmip database",
      "agu:nominatorCount": 3,
      "agu:citationCount": 7,
      "agu:reuseCount": 2,
      "description": "ARTMIP is the Atmospheric River Tracking Method Intercomparison Project. The goal of ARTMIP is to understand and quantify uncertainties in atmospheric river (AR) science based on choice of detection/tracking methodology. It is a large community effort with contributors across the globe including North and South America, Asia, Africa, and Australia, all of whom have volunteered their time to provide the community with data to understand and interpret scientific results. ARs are dynamically driven, filamentary structures often associated with extreme storms and heavy precipitation. ARTMIP provides a large set of AR catalogues, each created with a unique AR detection tool (ARDT). These catalogues are designed to be compared; metrics such as frequency, duration, and footprint can be consistently quantified across ARDTs using the same exact dataset. ARTMIP is divided into “Tier 1” and “Tier 2” where Tier 1 is the baseline control and consists of AR catalogues created using data generated from MERRA-2. Tier 2 includes a wide variety of sensitivity datasets and currently includes…",
      "url": "https://gdex.ucar.edu/datasets/d651012/",
      "creator": [
        {
