      "agu:justification": [
        {
          "@type": "CreativeWork",
          "agu:sequence": 1,
          "text": "ArcticDEM and REMA have transformed science capabilities in polar regions, which were among the least-mapped regions on Earth only a few years ago. These data enable a broad range of science activities, from measuring changes in glaciers and ice sheets to river hydrology and ecology. They also enable field work that would be otherwise impossible by allowing researchers to plan deployments and operations. The data’s practical applications impact the safety and prosperity of human communities. As of July 2025, the journal article describing REMA and the data citations for ArcticDEM and REMA have collectively been cited in 915 publications. Surface topography is among the most fundamental Earth Science data sets, essential to numerous research activities, including hazard assessment and mitigation, hydrologic modeling, solid earth dynamics, and many others. Change in surface topography…"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "Dataset",
      "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:dataset:agu-0019",
