      "agu:nominatorCount": 1,
      "agu:citationCount": 0,
      "agu:reuseCount": 1,
      "description": "The California Cooperative Oceanic Fisheries Investigations (CalCOFI) Bottle Database contains one of the longest and most comprehensive oceanographic time series in the world, spanning from 1949 to the present. It includes chemical and physical measurements from seawater samples collected at fixed stations throughout the California Current System off of California. Parameters include temperature, salinity, dissolved oxygen, chlorophyll-a, nutrients, and other oceanographic variables derived from bottle samples collected at discrete depths using Niskin bottles on a CTD-Rosette system. These data allow users to explore changes in water column structure, biogeochemistry, and productivity over time and are foundational for understanding long-term ocean variability, ecosystem change, and fisheries dynamics off the coast of California.",
      "url": "https://coastwatch.pfeg.noaa.gov/erddap/tabledap/siocalcofiHydroCast.html",
      "sameAs": [
        "https://calcofi.org/data/oceanographic-data/bottle-database/"
      ],
