      "name": "California Climate Projections",
      "alternateName": "",
      "keywords": {
        "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:theme:biosphere"
      },
      "agu:datasetId": "agu-0026",
      "agu:stableKey": "title:california climate projections",
      "agu:nominatorCount": 1,
      "agu:citationCount": 3,
      "agu:reuseCount": 1,
      "description": "Nominators 1a and 1b: The project produced four primary climate projection datasets. 1. Dynamically Downscaled Data: Eight CMIP6 GCMs were dynamically downscaled using the Weather Research and Forecasting (WRF) model to 9 km over the western U.S. and 3 km over California under SSP3-7.0. The dataset includes 30 hourly variables and additional 6-hourly outputs. Five models were bias-corrected before downscaling. 2. LOCA2-Hybrid: Fifteen CMIP6 GCMs were statistically downscaled to 3 km over California using dynamically downscaled data to capture weather and climate patterns. The LOCA2 (Localized Constructed Analogues) method (Pierce et al., J. of Hydrometeorology, 2023) applies bias correction throughout the statistical process and includes multiple SSPs and ensemble members from each GCM. Daily variables include temperature, precipitation, wind, humidity, and solar radiation, with hourly temperature downscaling at 32 stations. 3. Hydrologic Projections: Two hydrology models, Noah-MP (via WRF-Hydro) and VIC, simulated land-surface conditions using four dynamically downscaled and 18…",
      "url": "https://analytics.cal-adapt.org/data/",
      "creator": [
        {
          "@type": "Person",
          "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:person:dan-cayan-david-pierce-stefan-rahimi-benjamin-bass-lu-su-dennis-letten",
          "name": "Dan Cayan, David Pierce, Stefan Rahimi, Benjamin Bass, Lu Su, Dennis Lettenmaier, Alex Hall"
        }
      ],
      "agu:curator": [
        {
          "@type": "Person",
          "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:person:cal-adapt-analytics-engine",
