        "name": "Cal-Adapt Analytics Engine"
      },
      "citation": [
        {
          "@type": "CreativeWork",
          "text": "Nominators 1a and 1b: Additional information about the data can be found on the California Energy Commission's Website under \"Climate Change Assessment Data Summaries\" and \"Supporting Information for Data Summaries.\"…"
        },
        {
          "@type": "CreativeWork",
          "text": "Nominator 2 (for LOCA2-Hybrid): Pierce, D. W., Cayan, D. R., Feldman, D. R., & Risser, M. D. (2023). Future increases in north american extreme precipitation in cmip6 downscaled with loca. Journal of Hydrometeorology, 24(5), 951–975. https://doi.org/10.1175/JHM-D-22-0194.1"
        },
        {
          "@type": "CreativeWork",
          "text": "Pierce, D. W., Cayan, D. R., & Thrasher, B. L. (2014). Statistical downscaling using localized constructed analogs (Loca). Journal of Hydrometeorology, 15(6), 2558–2585. https://doi.org/10.1175/JHM-D-14-0082.1"
        }
      ],
      "agu:reuseExample": [
        {
          "@type": "CreativeWork",
          "text": "The data has been recently released, just over a year, so much of the work using the data is still in progress."
        }
      ],
      "agu:nominator": [
        {
          "@type": "Person",
          "@id": "https://orcid.org/0009-0006-0369-2059",
          "name": "Mark Koenig",
          "affiliation": {
            "@type": "Organization",
            "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:organization:eagle-rock-analytics-3669-57th-st-sacramento-ca-95820",
            "name": "Eagle Rock Analytics, 3669 57th St, Sacramento, CA 95820"
          },
          "agu:sequence": 1
        }
      ],
      "agu:justification": [
        {
          "@type": "CreativeWork",
          "agu:sequence": 1,
          "text": "Nominators 1a and 1b: The dataset was nominated because it represents a comprehensive, state-of-the-art climate data resource for California. A key innovation of this dataset is its hybrid-statistical downscaling approach, which combines the LOCA (Localized Constructed Analogs; Pierce et al., Journal of Hydrometeorology, 2023) statistical method with a pattern library derived from dynamically downscaled simulations that capture both historical and future climate conditions. This hybrid technique reduces the assumption of stationarity, the notion that future weather patterns will be the same as those of the past. By integrating dynamically and statistically downscaled datasets, California agencies, governments, and researchers gain access to high-temporal-resolution data along with projections spanning multiple future scenarios (SSPs), ensemble members, and global climate models (GCMs).…"
        }
      ]
    },
