      "name": "China Meteorological Forcing Dataset",
      "alternateName": "",
      "keywords": {
        "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:theme:atmos"
      },
      "agu:datasetId": "agu-0032",
      "agu:stableKey": "title:china meteorological forcing dataset",
      "agu:nominatorCount": 1,
      "agu:citationCount": 1,
      "agu:reuseCount": 6,
      "description": "China Meteorological Forcing Data (CMFD) is a high-precision, high-resolution, long-term dataset developed to support land surface, hydrology, and ecology research over China. The newly released CMFD 2.0 provides near-surface temperature, pressure, specific humidity, wind speed, downward shortwave and longwave radiation, and precipitation, with a temporal resolution of 3 hours, spatial resolution of 0.1°, and a 74-year span (1951–2024) covering 70°E–140°E, 15°N–55°N. CMFD 2.0 integrates ERA5 reanalysis with Chinese meteorological station observations, and applies AI-based products for radiation and precipitation, significantly improving accuracy over previous versions. CMFD 2.0 also provides derived variables (e.g., relative humidity, rain–snow separated precipitation).",
      "url": "https://data.tpdc.ac.cn/en/data/e60dfd96-5fd8-493f-beae-e8e5d24dece4",
      "creator": [
        {
          "@type": "Person",
