        },
        {
          "@type": "CreativeWork",
          "text": "Li, X., Liu, F., Ma, C., Hou, J., Zheng, D., Ma, H., Bai, Y., Han, X., Vereecken, H., Yang, K., Duan, Q., & Huang, C. (2024). Land data assimilation: Harmonizing theory and data in land surface…"
        },
        {
          "@type": "CreativeWork",
          "text": "Xu, F., Zhang, G., Woolway, R. I., Yang, K., Wada, Y., Wang, J., & Crétaux, J.-F. (2024). Widespread societal and ecological impacts from projected Tibetan Plateau lake expansion. Nature Geoscience,…"
        }
      ],
      "agu:nominator": [
        {
          "@type": "Person",
          "@id": "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5662-5435",
          "name": "Wenhao Dong",
          "affiliation": {
            "@type": "Organization",
            "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:organization:noaa-geophysical-fluid-dynamics-laboratory-201-forrestal-road-princeto",
            "name": "NOAA/Geophysical Fluid Dynamics Laboratory, 201 Forrestal Road, Princeton, NJ 08540"
          },
          "agu:sequence": 1
        }
      ],
      "agu:justification": [
        {
          "@type": "CreativeWork",
          "agu:sequence": 1,
          "text": "The China Meteorological Forcing Dataset (CMFD) is a transformative resource for both the scientific and broader community. Since its release, it has opened new frontiers in research, education, and applications across disciplines, serving as an exemplar of impactful open data. CMFD is widely used in education and training, with thousands of graduate students relying on it as a free and accessible dataset for studies in atmospheric science, hydrology, and ecology. The development team provides workshops and tutorials that lower barriers for early-career scientists. Beyond academia, CMFD contributes directly to disaster response and prediction. Its accurate meteorological inputs support early warning systems and improve forecasts of floods, droughts, and heatwaves, enabling communities to prepare and respond more effectively. CMFD has become indispensable for advancing understanding of…"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "Dataset",
      "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:dataset:agu-0033",
      "mainEntityOfPage": "https://impactfuldatasets.agu.org/#/dataset/agu-0033",
      "identifier": [
        {
          "@type": "PropertyValue",
          "propertyID": "AGU-Impactful-Datasets-ID",
          "value": "agu-0033"
        }
      ],
      "name": "Climate Ready DC: What does it mean to be Climate Ready?",
      "alternateName": "",
      "keywords": {
        "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:theme:society"
      },
      "agu:datasetId": "agu-0033",
      "agu:stableKey": "title:climate ready dc: what does it mean to be climate ready?",
      "agu:nominatorCount": 1,
      "agu:citationCount": 0,
      "agu:reuseCount": 0,
      "description": "This is a StoryMap of climate impacts in the District of Columbia. It incorporates engaging graphics, meaningful graphs (like how different generations experience heat in their lifetimes), local photos and a video, easy to digest information, and uplifting real-world solutions being implemented locally.",
      "url": "https://storymaps.arcgis.com/stories/fa9a73fc799249ffb206cbcd90231e8e",
      "creator": [
        {
          "@type": "Person",
          "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:person:erin-garnaas-holmes-at-the-dc-department-of-energy-and-environment",
          "name": "Erin Garnaas-Holmes at the DC Department of Energy and Environment"
        }
      ],
      "includedInDataCatalog": {
        "@type": "DataCatalog",
        "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:organization:department-of-energy-and-environment-website-https-doee-dc-gov-climate",
        "name": "Department of Energy and Environment website: https://doee.dc.gov/climateready"
      },
      "agu:nominator": [
        {
          "@type": "Person",
          "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:person:oana-leahu-aluas",
          "name": "Oana Leahu-Aluas",
          "affiliation": {
            "@type": "Organization",
            "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:organization:dc-department-of-energy-and-environment-1200-first-st-ne-washington-dc",
            "name": "DC Department of Energy and Environment, 1200 First St NE, Washington, DC 20002"
          },
          "agu:sequence": 1
        }
      ],
      "agu:justification": [
        {
          "@type": "CreativeWork",
          "agu:sequence": 1,
          "text": "This dataset is impactful because it centers people in discussing climate impacts. Traditional datasets showing plots on a graph are far removed from the everyday experiences of community members. The Climate Ready StoryMap provides an example to be emulated by jurisdictions around the world. This StoryMap is used to talk to 6th graders about climate impacts in DC and showing the flooding video that is embedded in the StoryMap and asking them to think how old they will be in 2030 or 2050 (corresponding to the chart showing extreme heat days in those years), attracted a lot of attention and engagement from the students. The use of local photos and visuals with people frequently included drives home the point that climate change is not an impact separate from ourselves. Humans are an integral part of it and are impacted by it in very real ways."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "Dataset",
      "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:dataset:agu-0034",
      "mainEntityOfPage": "https://impactfuldatasets.agu.org/#/dataset/agu-0034",
      "identifier": [
        {
          "@type": "PropertyValue",
          "propertyID": "AGU-Impactful-Datasets-ID",
          "value": "agu-0034"
        }
      ],
      "name": "Community Earth Models",
      "alternateName": "",
      "keywords": {
        "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:theme:interior"
      },
      "agu:datasetId": "agu-0034",
      "agu:stableKey": "title:community earth models",
      "agu:nominatorCount": 1,
      "agu:citationCount": 0,
      "agu:reuseCount": 0,
      "description": "COMMUNITY EARTH MODELS aim to unify diverse data and expertise to build high-resolution models of key features of the lithosphere and asthenosphere for investigating seismic phenomena in California and beyond. CEMs are collaborative platforms featuring community-contributed data, models, and tools for earthquake system analysis. They enable 3D visualization, data exploration, sharing, and integrated modeling. The Statewide California Earthquake Center (SCEC) hosts and develops Community Earth Models (CEMs) that describe the lithosphere and asthenosphere of California and surrounding regions. These models provide an integrated framework for researchers wishing to simulate or study various earthquake-related phenomena throughout the entire Pacific-North American Plate boundary system. Each model is developed by a group of experts using diverse methods and data, with input from various user groups. SCEC’s CEMs are powerful tools for researchers, educators, and anyone interested in earthquakes. We encourage you to explore these valuable resources and integrate them into your work. Text…",
      "url": "https://www.scec.org/science/community-earth-models/",
      "creator": [
        {
          "@type": "Person",
          "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:person:becker-t-behr-w-bekaert-d-bird-p-chapman-d-cooke-m-fielding-e-j-floyd",
          "name": "Becker, T., Behr, W. Bekaert, D., Bird, P., Chapman, D., Cooke, M., Fielding, E., J. Floyd, Funning, G., González Ortega, A., Govorcin, M., Guns, K., Hardebeck, J., Hauksson, E., Hearn, E., Herring, T., Hirth, G., Houston, H., Johnson, K., Kreemer, C., Liu, Z., Loveless, J., Luttrell, K., Maechling, P. J., Marshall, S., Materna, K., Meade, B., Montesi, L., Oskin, M.,Plesch, A., Prejean, S., Sangha, S., Shaw, M., Shen, Z.-K., Shen, Z., Shinevar, W., Skoumal, R., Small, P. E. Smith-Konter, B., Su, M.-H Thatcher, W., Tymofyeyeva, E., Wang, K., & Xu, X., Yang, W., & Zeng, Y"
        }
      ],
      "agu:curator": [
