            "name": "Eawag / University of Zurich, Überlandstrasse 133, CH-8600 Dübendorf, Switzerland"
          },
          "agu:sequence": 1
        }
      ],
      "agu:justification": [
        {
          "@type": "CreativeWork",
          "agu:sequence": 1,
          "text": "The EStreams dataset and catalogue mark a major step forward for hydrological science in Europe, bridging the gap between fragmented national archives and global hydrological initiatives. While global repositories provide invaluable resources, they often lack detailed catchment metadata, consistent temporal coverage, and dense spatial representation across Europe. National-scale CAMELS-type datasets have revolutionized regional hydrology but remain confined within borders, limiting cross-country comparisons. EStreams overcomes these barriers through a harmonized, continental-scale framework integrating streamflow indices, hydro-climatic signatures, meteorological time series, and landscape descriptors from 1900 to 2022. Covering more than 17,000 catchments across 41 countries, EStreams enables exploration of streamflow variability, hydrological extremes, and long-term climate-driven…"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "Dataset",
      "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:dataset:agu-0041",
      "mainEntityOfPage": "https://impactfuldatasets.agu.org/#/dataset/agu-0041",
