      "name": "GeoNet (NZ) Geohazard Monitoring Datasets",
      "alternateName": "",
      "keywords": {
        "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:theme:surface"
      },
      "agu:datasetId": "agu-0047",
      "agu:stableKey": "title:geonet (nz) geohazard monitoring datasets",
      "agu:nominatorCount": 1,
      "agu:citationCount": 6,
      "agu:reuseCount": 9,
      "description": "Aotearoa New Zealand is one of the most geologically active countries in the world, and since 2001 GeoNet has been New Zealand’s national land and geohazards monitoring system delivering free and open data and information for geohazard monitoring and research across earthquakes, tsunami, landslides, volcanoes and deformation. GeoNet operates a multiparametric network of monitoring stations and a data collection, processing and dissemination infrastructure. The GeoNet programme is a conduit for science advice related to geohazard monitoring. “GeoNet data” encompasses a diverse data repository that include raw, processed and highly derived data products, that span from the New Zealand National Earthquake Catalogue and associated raw waveform data, to highly derived science products (e.g. Volcano Alert Levels). GeoNet datasets overlap in their utility and are truly multi-disciplinary and this range of hazard monitoring data and information are available through the website www.geonet.org.nz, a diverse array of access mechanisms and the GeoNet mobile phone application. A list of…",
      "creator": [
        {
