      "agu:justification": [
        {
          "@type": "CreativeWork",
          "agu:sequence": 1,
          "text": "The impact of the GeoReM database is predicated on a fundamental principle of chemical analysis in the fields of geochemistry and environmental chemistry: the utilization of (certified) reference materials. These materials form the basis for the traceability and comparability of all data determined by chemical analysis and used for scientific and administrative decision-making processes and economic evaluations. The database contains reference materials and their certified and preferred values, as well as published analytical data on these reference materials. The utilization of the database facilitates a multifaceted evaluation of the analytical methods employed, the technical capabilities of these methods, the sample preparation methods utilized, the laboratories conducting the analyses, and the time period over which the analyses were conducted. The database has been developed to…"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "Dataset",
      "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:dataset:agu-0049",
