      ],
      "agu:justification": [
        {
          "@type": "CreativeWork",
          "agu:sequence": 1,
          "text": "Because of the methodological advances underlying the production of this dataset, it is the first, and until now only, urban land change dataset specifically designed for understanding long-term human-Earth system interactions across spatial scales. It has been used broadly by researchers, practitioners, and students globally. As the corresponding author of the dataset, I receive frequent contacts regarding the data from a wide range of people. Recent inquires/users include, for example, a start-up company in Japan, college students in Indonesia, investigative journalists from UK, local government analysts in the U.S., etc. The dataset can be used in coordination with a closely related dataset produced by the same author, \"Global 1-km Downscaled Population Grids, SSP-Consistent Projections and Base Year, v1.01 (2000 - 2100)\" ( https://doi.org/10.7910/DVN/TLJ99B ), to investigate how…"
        }
      ]
