          "value": "https://doi.org/10.17605/OSF.IO/W4UG8"
        }
      ],
      "name": "Global Reservoir Inventory of Lost Storage by Sedimentation (GRILSS)",
      "alternateName": "",
      "keywords": {
        "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:theme:ocean"
      },
      "agu:datasetId": "agu-0057",
      "agu:stableKey": "doi:10.17605/osf.io/w4ug8|global reservoir inventory of lost storage by sedimentation (grilss)",
      "agu:nominatorCount": 1,
      "agu:citationCount": 1,
      "agu:reuseCount": 2,
      "description": "The Global Reservoir Inventory of Lost Storage by Sedimentation (GRILSS) dataset provides open-source data on sedimentation and capacity loss for 1,013 reservoirs in 75 major river basins across 54 countries. This dataset serves as a critical resource for studying reservoir sedimentation, which affects the storage capacity of artificial reservoirs, with implications for water management, environmental sustainability, and infrastructure planning. The dataset consists of two main components: sedimentation data and spatial vector data, allowing for detailed geospatial analysis of reservoirs, dams, and catchments worldwide. The data is intended to support sediment management strategies, research, and future contributions from the community. (reference: https://osf.io/w4ug8/)",
      "url": "https://doi.org/10.17605/OSF.IO/W4UG8",
      "creator": [
        {
          "@type": "Person",
          "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:person:sanchit-minocha-and-faisal-hossain",
          "name": "Sanchit Minocha and Faisal Hossain"
        }
      ],
      "agu:curator": [
        {
          "@type": "Person",
          "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:person:sanchit-minocha-and-faisal-hossain",
          "name": "Sanchit Minocha and Faisal Hossain"
        }
      ],
      "includedInDataCatalog": {
        "@type": "DataCatalog",
        "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:organization:open-science-framework-osf",
        "name": "Open Science Framework (OSF)"
      },
      "citation": [
        {
          "@type": "CreativeWork",
          "text": "Minocha, S., & Hossain, F. (2025). GRILSS: Opening the gateway to global reservoir sedimentation data curation. Earth System Science Data, 17(4), 1743–1759. https://doi.org/10.5194/essd-17-1743-2025"
        }
      ],
      "agu:reuseExample": [
        {
          "@type": "CreativeWork",
          "text": "The GRILSS dataset has already been reused in several independent studies, demonstrating its broad applicability and scientific value. For example, Suresh and Hossain (2025) used GRILSS to…"
        },
        {
          "@type": "CreativeWork",
          "text": "Within just a few months of its release, GRILSS has been cited in multiple peer-reviewed publications, reflecting its growing role as a foundational dataset for global research on reservoir…"
        }
      ],
      "agu:nominator": [
        {
          "@type": "Person",
          "@id": "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-1969-7521",
          "name": "Sanchit Minocha",
          "affiliation": {
            "@type": "Organization",
            "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:organization:university-of-washington-1400-ne-campus-parkway-seattle-wa-98195",
            "name": "University of Washington, 1400 NE Campus Parkway, Seattle, WA 98195"
          },
          "agu:sequence": 1
        }
      ],
      "agu:justification": [
        {
          "@type": "CreativeWork",
          "agu:sequence": 1,
          "text": "Reservoirs are the backbone of global water security. They store water for drinking, farming, and energy generation, and help control floods and droughts. But across the world, many reservoirs are slowly losing their storage capacity as sediments carried by rivers settle inside them. This process, called reservoir sedimentation, quietly reduces how much water a reservoir can hold. The problem has been known for decades, yet the world has lacked a reliable, open dataset to understand how serious it is, where it is happening fastest, and how it is changing over time. The Global Reservoir Inventory of Lost Storage by Sedimentation (GRILSS) dataset fills this critical gap. It is the first global, openly available dataset that measures how much water storage has been lost in reservoirs due to sedimentation. Impact on People: When reservoirs lose storage, people face water shortages, higher…"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
