          "@type": "Person",
          "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:person:andreas-p-ahlstr-m",
          "name": "Andreas P. Ahlstrøm"
        }
      ],
      "includedInDataCatalog": {
        "@type": "DataCatalog",
        "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:organization:dataverse-geus-dk",
        "name": "dataverse.geus.dk"
      },
      "citation": [
        {
          "@type": "CreativeWork",
          "text": "https://essd.copernicus.org/articles/12/2811/2020/ (73 listed)"
        }
      ],
      "agu:reuseExample": [
        {
          "@type": "CreativeWork",
          "text": "A selection of different topics:"
        },
        {
          "@type": "CreativeWork",
          "text": "Kanna, N., Sugiyama, S., Ando, T., Wang, Y., Sakuragi, Y., Hazumi, T., Matsuno, K., Yamaguchi, A., Nishioka, J., & Yamashita, Y. (2022). Meltwater discharge from marine‐terminating glaciers drives…"
        },
        {
          "@type": "CreativeWork",
          "text": "Lindeman, M. R., Straneo, F., Adams, H. M., Nelson, M. J. S., & Schartup, A. T. (2024). Low mercury concentrations in a Greenland glacial fjord attributed to oceanic sources. Communications Earth &…"
        },
        {
          "@type": "CreativeWork",
          "text": "Wood, M., Carroll, D., Fenty, I., Bertin, C., Darby, B., Dutkiewicz, S., Hopwood, M., Khazendar, A., Meire, L., Oliver, H., Parker, T., & Willis, J. (2025). Increased melt from Greenland’s most…"
        },
        {
          "@type": "CreativeWork",
          "text": "Hansen, K., Karlsson, N. B., How, P., Poulsen, E., Mortensen, J., & Rysgaard, S. (2025). Winter subglacial meltwater detected in a Greenland fjord. Nature Geoscience, 18(3), 219–225.…"
        }
      ],
      "agu:nominator": [
        {
          "@type": "Person",
          "@id": "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9743-079X",
          "name": "Mark James Hopwood",
          "affiliation": {
            "@type": "Organization",
            "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:organization:southern-university-of-science-and-technology-1088-xueyuan-avenue-nans",
            "name": "Southern University of Science and Technology, 1088 Xueyuan Avenue, Nanshan District, Shenzhen, Guangdong Province, China, 518055"
          },
          "agu:sequence": 1
        }
      ],
      "agu:justification": [
        {
          "@type": "CreativeWork",
          "agu:sequence": 1,
          "text": "Knowing the volume and distribution of freshwater discharge from the Greenland Ice Sheet is essential for understanding its implications for global sea level rise, regional and global ocean circulation, coastal hazards, and marine ecosystems. Before Mankoff et al. developed a quality-controlled dataset that provided an estimate of discharge from every catchment in Greenland, there was nothing close to such data product and so all estimates of discharge volume and its distribution were crude and disharmonious across the literature. In most cases, it simply was not possible to deduce the effects of meltwater in the ocean. The development of a high-quality, high-resolution estimate of runoff allowed a step forward in multiple fields, concerning how this freshwater drives changes in the Earth System. We know that landslides around Greenland, and tidal tsunamis are triggered by discharge…"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "Dataset",
      "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:dataset:agu-0064",
