      "name": "Gridded Population of the World (GPW)",
      "alternateName": "",
      "keywords": {
        "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:theme:society"
      },
      "agu:datasetId": "agu-0064",
      "agu:stableKey": "doi:10.7927/h4np22dq|gridded population of the world (gpw)",
      "agu:nominatorCount": 1,
      "agu:citationCount": 1,
      "agu:reuseCount": 1,
      "description": "The Gridded Population of the World (GPW), CIESIN's flagship data product and truly a foundational data set in the Earth sciences, was first released in 1998 via the NASA Socioeconomic Data and Applications Center (SEDAC). It was the first globally gridded data set of population, developed with the intention of facilitating data integration across the Earth and social sciences. It has been used in countless studies related to population exposure to environmental hazards, the distribution of populations at risk to various diseases, and simple counts of population according to various geographies, among other things. It has also been the foundation for a range of products such as the PLACE data set (which provides population estimates by biome, elevation zone, etc.) as well as a series of modeled population data sets (GRUMP, GHS-POP, WorldPop, etc.) . GPW versions 3 and 4, the last two published, have been cited thousands of times in the Earth science, hazards, and public health literature. GPWv4, the most recent version (version 5 is under production), consists of estimates of human…",
      "url": "https://doi.org/10.7927/H4NP22DQ",
