        {
          "@type": "CreativeWork",
          "agu:sequence": 1,
          "text": "Without GPW, we would not understand how many people are affected by a whole range of environmental phenomena. GPW was used in epidemiological models for the spread of COVID. For a better sense of the applications and the pathbreaking nature of GPW, see: de Sherbinin, A. (2017). Remote sensing and socioeconomic data integration: Lessons from the NASA Socioeconomic Data and Applications Center. In D. A. Quattrochi, E. Wentz, N. N. Lam, & C. Emerson (Eds.), Integrating scale in remote sensing and GIS (pp. 371–387). CRC Press. https://www.taylorfrancis.com/chapters/edit/10.1201/9781315373720-23/remote-sensing-socioeconomic-data-integration-lessons-nasa-socioeconomic-data-applications-center-alex-de-sherbinin Leaving No One Off the Map: A Guide for Gridded Population Data for Sustainable Development. https://www.popgrid.org/sites/default/files/documents/Leaving_no_one_off_the_map.pdf"
        }
      ]
    },
