          "value": "agu-0067"
        },
        {
          "@type": "PropertyValue",
          "propertyID": "DOI",
          "value": "https://doi.org/10.5061/dryad.vq83bk42w"
        }
      ],
      "name": "HarvestStat Africa",
      "alternateName": "",
      "keywords": {
        "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:theme:biosphere"
      },
      "agu:datasetId": "agu-0067",
      "agu:stableKey": "doi:10.5061/dryad.vq83bk42w|harveststat africa",
      "agu:nominatorCount": 1,
      "agu:citationCount": 2,
      "agu:reuseCount": 3,
      "description": "HarvestStat Africa presents the largest compilation of open-access subnational crop statistics and time-series across Sub-Saharan Africa. Based on agricultural statistics collated by USAID’s Famine Early Warning Systems Network, the subnational crop statistics are standardized and calibrated across changing administrative units to produce consistent and continuous time-series. The dataset includes 574,204 records, primarily spanning from 1980 to 2022, detailing quantity produced, harvested areas, and yields for 33 countries and 94 crop types, including key cereals in Sub-Saharan Africa such as wheat, maize, rice, sorghum, barley, millet, and fonio. This new dataset enhances our understanding of how climate variability and change influence agricultural production, supports subnational food system analysis, and aids in operational yield forecasting. As an open-source resource, it establishes a precedent for sharing subnational crop statistics to inform decision-making and modeling efforts",
      "url": "https://doi.org/10.5061/dryad.vq83bk42w",
      "sameAs": [
        "https://datadryad.org/dataset/doi:10.5061/dryad.vq83bk42w",
        "https://www-nature-com.proxy-um.researchport.umd.edu/articles/s41597-025-05001-z#Sec11"
      ],
      "creator": [
        {
          "@type": "Person",
          "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:person:donghoon-lee-weston-anderson-and-co-authors",
          "name": "Donghoon Lee, Weston Anderson, and co-authors"
        }
      ],
      "agu:curator": [
        {
          "@type": "Person",
          "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:person:weston-anderson-donghoon-lee-fews-net-harveststat-https-www-harveststa",
          "name": "Weston Anderson, Donghoon Lee, FEWS NET, HarvestStat (https://www.harveststat.org/)"
        }
      ],
      "includedInDataCatalog": {
        "@type": "DataCatalog",
        "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:organization:dryad",
        "name": "Dryad"
      },
      "citation": [
        {
          "@type": "CreativeWork",
          "text": "https://www-nature-com.proxy-um.researchport.umd.edu/articles/s41597-025-05001-z#Sec11"
        },
        {
          "@type": "CreativeWork",
          "text": "Davis, K. F., Anderson, W., Ehrmann, S., Flach, R., Meyer, C., Proctor, J., Ray, D., You, L., Foley, M., Kerdiles, H., Hultgren, A., Huybers, P., Kebede, E., Meroni, M., Park, C., & Lee, D. (2025). HarvestStat: A global effort towards open and standardized sub-national agricultural data.…"
        }
      ],
      "agu:reuseExample": [
        {
          "@type": "CreativeWork",
          "text": "Davenport, F., Lee, D., Shukla, S., Husak, G., Funk, C., Budde, M., & Rowland, J. (2024). Testing spatial out-of-sample area of influence for grain forecasting models. Environmental Research Letters,…"
        },
        {
          "@type": "CreativeWork",
          "text": "https://www-nature-com.proxy-um.researchport.umd.edu/articles/s41597-025-05257-5"
        },
        {
          "@type": "CreativeWork",
          "text": "https://www-nature-com.proxy-um.researchport.umd.edu/articles/s41597-024-04313-w"
        }
      ],
      "agu:nominator": [
        {
          "@type": "Person",
          "@id": "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3755-9943",
          "name": "Weston Anderson",
          "affiliation": {
            "@type": "Organization",
            "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:organization:university-of-maryland",
            "name": "University of Maryland"
          },
          "agu:sequence": 1
        }
      ],
      "agu:justification": [
        {
          "@type": "CreativeWork",
          "agu:sequence": 1,
          "text": "This dataset is impactful because HarvestStat Africa improves understanding of how climate variability and change influence agricultural production, supports subnational food system analysis, and aids in operational yield forecasting. HarvestStat Africa is already being used to produce subnational crop forecasts for the Famine Early Warning Systems Network (FEWS NET), the UN Food and Agriculture Organization Global Information and Early Warning System, NASA Harvest, and the Joint Research Centre of the European Commission. As a first-of-its-kind open-source subnational crop production dataset, it establishes a precedent for sharing subnational crop statistics to inform decision-making and modeling efforts. The data, methods, and community continue to grow and evolve as more organizations and individuals are becoming involved in the HarvestStat effort."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "Dataset",
      "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:dataset:agu-0068",
      "mainEntityOfPage": "https://impactfuldatasets.agu.org/#/dataset/agu-0068",
      "identifier": [
        {
          "@type": "PropertyValue",
          "propertyID": "AGU-Impactful-Datasets-ID",
          "value": "agu-0068"
        },
        {
          "@type": "PropertyValue",
          "propertyID": "DOI",
          "value": "https://doi.org/10.7910/DVN/VGSN7Q"
        }
      ],
      "name": "Historical Bolide Infrasound Dataset (1960-1972)",
      "alternateName": "",
      "keywords": {
        "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:theme:space"
      },
      "agu:datasetId": "agu-0068",
      "agu:stableKey": "doi:10.7910/dvn/vgsn7q|historical bolide infrasound dataset (1960-1972)",
      "agu:nominatorCount": 1,
      "agu:citationCount": 1,
      "agu:reuseCount": 2,
      "description": "This dataset is the first fully curated, publicly accessible archive of infrasonic records from ten large bolide events documented by the U.S. Air Force Technical Applications Center's global microbarometer network between 1960 and 1972. These waveforms, originally captured on analog strip-chart paper, predate modern digital arrays and space-based sensors, making them a unique window on meteoroid activity in the mid-twentieth century. Prior studies drew scientific conclusions from these records but released only limited artifacts, such as period-amplitude tables or unprocessed scans, leaving the underlying data inaccessible for independent study. This release transforms those limited excerpts into a research-ready resource. It constitutes a critical reference point for assessing bolide activity before the advent of modern monitoring and provides a valuable reference for comparing past and present detections, facilitating assessments of long-term flux and acoustic wave propagation. The dataset's consolidated format supports a wide range of scientific inquiries, establishing a basis…",
      "url": "https://doi.org/10.7910/DVN/VGSN7Q",
      "creator": [
        {
          "@type": "Person",
          "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:person:elizabeth-a-silber-and-rodney-w-whitaker",
          "name": "Elizabeth A. Silber and Rodney W. Whitaker"
        }
      ],
      "agu:curator": [
        {
          "@type": "Person",
          "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:person:elizabeth-a-silber-and-rodney-w-whitaker",
          "name": "Elizabeth A. Silber and Rodney W. Whitaker"
        }
      ],
      "includedInDataCatalog": {
        "@type": "DataCatalog",
        "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:organization:harvard-dataverse",
        "name": "Harvard Dataverse"
      },
      "citation": [
        {
          "@type": "CreativeWork",
          "text": "Silber, E. A., & Whitaker, R. W. (2025). Historical bolide infrasound dataset(1960–1972). Data, 10(5), 71. https://doi.org/10.3390/data10050071"
        }
      ],
      "agu:reuseExample": [
        {
          "@type": "CreativeWork",
          "text": "Milliken KL, Ergene SM, Ozkan A."
        },
        {
          "@type": "CreativeWork",
          "text": "2016. Quartz types, authigenic and detrital, in the Upper Cretaceous Eagle Ford Formation, south Texas, USA. Sedimentary Geology 339:273–288. https://doi.org/10.1016/j.sedgeo.2016.03.012"
        }
      ],
      "agu:nominator": [
        {
          "@type": "Person",
          "@id": "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4778-1409",
          "name": "Elizabeth A. Silber",
          "affiliation": {
            "@type": "Organization",
            "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:organization:sandia-national-laboratories-1515-eubank-blvd-se-albuquerque-nm-87123",
            "name": "Sandia National Laboratories, 1515 Eubank Blvd SE, Albuquerque, NM 87123, USA"
          },
          "agu:sequence": 1
        }
      ],
      "agu:justification": [
        {
          "@type": "CreativeWork",
          "agu:sequence": 1,
          "text": "This dataset is uniquely impactful because it rescues, curates, and makes accessible an irreplaceable record of Earth's interaction with near-Earth objects (NEOs) from an era (1960-1972) that predates modern space-based and digital monitoring. Without this fully curated dataset, researchers could not independently verify historical bolide energy estimates, compare legacy analog instrumentation with modern digital networks, or access the underlying calibrated waveform data from these ten major events. Planet Dimension: The dataset provides a fundamental baseline for planetary science, capturing ground-truth measurements of bolide activity during a period with sparse observations. It fills a critical gap in the NEO influx database, allowing for refined meteoroid flux models and long-term comparisons of bolide frequencies and magnitudes. It directly supports the study of geophysical…",
          "agu:impactDimension": [
            {
              "@type": "DefinedTerm",
              "name": "Planet",
              "description": "The dataset provides a fundamental baseline for planetary science, capturing ground-truth measurements of bolide activity during a period with sparse observations. It fills a critical gap in the NEO influx database, allowing for refined meteoroid flux models and long-term comparisons of bolide frequencies and magnitudes. It directly supports the study of geophysical phenomena, including meteoroid fragmentation and…"
            },
            {
              "@type": "DefinedTerm",
              "name": "People",
              "description": "This release transforms previously inaccessible artifacts (analog strip-charts and limited raw scans) into a research-ready, FAIR-compliant archive. For the first time, it provides cleaned images, geometrically straightened traces, calibrated pressure-time files, and the digitized instrument-response function. This empowers a new generation of researchers by enabling independent study, reproducible reanalysis, and…"
            },
            {
              "@type": "DefinedTerm",
              "name": "Prosperity",
              "description": "The data directly supports planetary defense and community resilience. By establishing a historical baseline for meter-to-tens-of-meter scale impacts, the dataset provides important data points for refining impact hazard evaluations and bolide energy-scaling laws. This improved understanding of NEO impact frequency and energy is essential for assessing and mitigating future impact risks, which carry profound…"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "Dataset",
      "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:dataset:agu-0069",
      "mainEntityOfPage": "https://impactfuldatasets.agu.org/#/dataset/agu-0069",
      "identifier": [
        {
          "@type": "PropertyValue",
          "propertyID": "AGU-Impactful-Datasets-ID",
          "value": "agu-0069"
        },
        {
          "@type": "PropertyValue",
          "propertyID": "DOI",
          "value": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.14996262"
        }
      ],
      "name": "Historical daily discharge data of Italian rivers - SIREN project",
      "alternateName": "",
      "keywords": {
        "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:theme:ocean"
      },
      "agu:datasetId": "agu-0069",
      "agu:stableKey": "doi:10.5281/zenodo.14996262|historical daily discharge data of italian rivers - siren project",
      "agu:nominatorCount": 1,
      "agu:citationCount": 1,
      "agu:reuseCount": 0,
      "description": "The dataset consists of digitized historical daily river flow measurements from across Italy, originally collected and published throughout the 20th century by the Italian national hydrological service in the volumes of the hydrological yearbooks. These yearbooks represent a unique and invaluable archive of hydrological observations, but until now they were only available in printed form, making their use extremely difficult for scientific, engineering, and policy applications. Through the SIREN (Saving Italian hydRological mEasuremeNts) citizen science project, thousands of volunteers from around the world contributed to transcribing more than 17,000 tables of daily discharge data, each containing 365 values. Each record was digitized independently by at least two volunteers, with discrepancies resolved through manual quality control by the project team. This process has produced a high-quality, machine-readable dataset that follows the FAIR principles (Findable, Accessible, Interoperable, Reusable). The dataset provides a consistent and openly available record of Italian river…",
      "url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.14996262",
      "creator": [
        {
          "@type": "Person",
          "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:person:paola-mazzoglio-miriam-bertola",
          "name": "Paola Mazzoglio, Miriam Bertola"
        }
      ],
      "agu:curator": [
        {
          "@type": "Person",
          "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:person:paola-mazzoglio",
          "name": "Paola Mazzoglio"
        }
      ],
      "includedInDataCatalog": {
        "@type": "DataCatalog",
        "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:organization:zenodo",
        "name": "Zenodo"
      },
      "citation": [
        {
          "@type": "CreativeWork",
          "text": "https://doi.org/10.5194/egusphere-egu25-1395 and https://doi.org/10.5194/egusphere-egu24-2080 (a datapaper is planned to be prepared and submitted in late 2025)."
        }
      ],
      "agu:nominator": [
        {
          "@type": "Person",
          "@id": "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3662-9439",
          "name": "Paola Mazzoglio",
          "affiliation": {
            "@type": "Organization",
            "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:organization:politecnico-di-torino-10129-torino-italy",
            "name": "Politecnico di Torino, 10129 Torino, Italy"
          },
          "agu:sequence": 1
        }
      ],
      "agu:justification": [
        {
          "@type": "CreativeWork",
          "agu:sequence": 1,
          "text": "The SIREN dataset represents the first comprehensive effort to digitize and make openly available historical daily river discharge measurements across Italy. Originally collected and published in printed Hydrological Yearbooks by the former National Hydrographic and Mareographic Service (SIMN) throughout the 20th century, these data have until now been largely inaccessible to the scientific and policy communities. Their release fills a critical gap, aligning Italy with other European countries that already benefit from digitized hydrological archives. People dimension. The dataset enhances education and science by providing a rich resource for students, researchers, and citizens. It raises public awareness of the importance of long-term hydrological monitoring and creates opportunities for active participation in science, as thousands of volunteers contributed to its digitization. It…"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "Dataset",
      "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:dataset:agu-0070",
      "mainEntityOfPage": "https://impactfuldatasets.agu.org/#/dataset/agu-0070",
      "identifier": [
        {
          "@type": "PropertyValue",
          "propertyID": "AGU-Impactful-Datasets-ID",
          "value": "agu-0070"
