      "agu:nominatorCount": 1,
      "agu:citationCount": 2,
      "agu:reuseCount": 2,
      "description": "This dataset includes hourly estimates of sea surface temperature and near-surface ocean currents derived from the data collected by satellite-tracked surface drifting buoys, or drifters, of the NOAA Global Drifter Program. These estimates are currently derived by the Drifter Data Assembly Center (DAC) of the NOAA’s Atlantic Oceanographic and Meteorological Laboratory (AOML) in Miami, following the methodologies described in two peer-reviewed papers which were led by the nominator. The principal data consist of 19 different variables, including positions (latitude and longitude), ocean velocities (eastward, northward), and sea surface temperatures (SST; total, diurnal, and non-diurnal components) with accompanying uncertainty estimates, along the trajectories of drifters, at hourly intervals. The associated metadata consist of 39 variables, including identification and experiment numbers, deployment and death dates and times, and various specific information related to drifter types, characteristics, and manufacturers. The latest release of the dataset (version 2.01.1) contains the…",
      "url": "https://doi.org/10.25921/x46c-3620",
