      "agu:stableKey": "doi:10.5281/zenodo.4065266|improved italian - rainfall extreme dataset (i2-red)",
      "agu:nominatorCount": 1,
      "agu:citationCount": 1,
      "agu:reuseCount": 7,
      "description": "Obtaining hydrological information in Italy is challenging. After the dismantlement of the national hydrological service performed more than 30 years ago, data collection and management were transferred to 21 regional authorities. Each adopted different data policies, despite national law requiring public data to be openly available for research and non-profit purposes. As of 2025, some agencies still do not publish rainfall data online and release them only upon request, often in tables or PDFs. Moreover, most historical series remain available solely in printed Hydrological Yearbooks. The Improved Italian - Rainfall Extreme Dataset (I²-RED) was developed to address this gap by providing a homogeneous, nationwide archive to support analyses of frequency, spatial distribution, and long-term evolution of extreme rainfall. It collects annual maximum rainfall depths for 1, 3, 6, 12, and 24 hours from more than 5000 gauges operating in Italy since 1916. Station coordinates and altitudes were checked against the EU-DEM elevation model, with large inconsistencies corrected. Internal…",
      "url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.4065266",
      "creator": [
        {
          "@type": "Person",
          "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:person:paola-mazzoglio-ilaria-butera-pierluigi-claps",
