          "name": "James Acker",
          "affiliation": {
            "@type": "Organization",
            "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:organization:nasa-goddard-earth-sciences-data-and-information-services-center-ges-d",
            "name": "NASA Goddard Earth Sciences Data and Information Services Center (GES DISC), NASA Goddard Space Flight Center, 8800 Greenbelt Rd, Greenbelt, MD 20771, USA"
          },
          "agu:sequence": 1
        }
      ],
      "agu:justification": [
        {
          "@type": "CreativeWork",
          "agu:sequence": 1,
          "text": "The capability of gaining a more detailed understanding of Earth’s interconnected natural systems – encompassing physical and biological phenomena which take place in the atmosphere, oceans, and diverse land environments ranging from ice sheets to tropical rainforests – and also to examine their multitude of interactions – was markedly changed by satellite remote-sensing data. No longer restricted to data collected in single locations or small regions, researchers extended their viewpoint over altitude, latitude, and longitude, observing large-scale events and processes over their entire range of influence. As an example, detection of the occurrence of tropical cyclones far from land was significantly enhanced, allowing better prediction of potential risk, as well as improved understanding of factors contributing to their strength and movement. Many variables are likely needed to…"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "Dataset",
      "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:dataset:agu-0086",
      "mainEntityOfPage": "https://impactfuldatasets.agu.org/#/dataset/agu-0086",
      "identifier": [
        {
          "@type": "PropertyValue",
          "propertyID": "AGU-Impactful-Datasets-ID",
          "value": "agu-0086"
        }
      ],
      "name": "NASA Earth Exchange Global Daily Downscaled Projections (NEX-GDDP) CMIP5 & CMIP 6",
      "alternateName": "",
      "keywords": {
        "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:theme:atmos"
      },
      "agu:datasetId": "agu-0086",
      "agu:stableKey": "title:nasa earth exchange global daily downscaled projections (nex-gddp) cmip5 & cmip 6",
      "agu:nominatorCount": 1,
      "agu:citationCount": 1,
      "agu:reuseCount": 0,
      "description": "The NEX-GDDP-CMIP6 dataset is comprised of global downscaled climate scenarios derived from the General Circulation Model (GCM) runs conducted under the Coupled Model Intercomparison Project Phase 6 (CMIP6) and across all four “Tier 1” greenhouse gas emissions scenarios known as Shared Socioeconomic Pathways (SSPs). The CMIP6 GCM runs were developed in support of the Sixth Assessment Report of the Intergovernmental Panel on Climate Change (IPCC AR6). This dataset includes downscaled projections from ScenarioMIP model runs for which daily scenarios were produced and distributed through the Earth System Grid Federation. The purpose of this dataset is to provide a set of global, high resolution, bias-corrected climate change projections that can be used to evaluate climate change impacts on processes that are sensitive to finer-scale climate gradients and the effects of local topography on climate conditions.",
      "url": "https://www.nccs.nasa.gov/services/data-collections/land-based-products/nex-gddp-cmip6",
      "creator": [
        {
          "@type": "Person",
          "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:person:bridget-thrasher",
          "name": "Bridget Thrasher"
        }
      ],
      "includedInDataCatalog": {
        "@type": "DataCatalog",
        "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:organization:nccs",
        "name": "NCCS"
      },
      "citation": [
        {
          "@type": "CreativeWork",
          "text": "Thrasher, B., Wang, W., Michaelis, A., Melton, F., Lee, T., & Nemani, R. (2022). Nasa global daily downscaled projections, CMIP6. Scientific Data, 9(1), 262. https://doi.org/10.1038/s41597-022-01393-4"
        }
      ],
      "agu:nominator": [
        {
          "@type": "Person",
          "@id": "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2509-4325",
          "name": "Ian Brosnan",
          "affiliation": {
            "@type": "Organization",
            "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:organization:nasa-ames-research-center-po-box-1-moffett-field-ca-94035-1000",
            "name": "NASA Ames Research Center, PO Box 1, Moffett Field, CA 94035-1000"
          },
          "agu:sequence": 1
        }
      ],
      "agu:justification": [
        {
          "@type": "CreativeWork",
          "agu:sequence": 1,
          "text": "NEX-GDDP-CMIP6 (and its CMIP5 version) is one of the most widely used and impactful downscaled climate projections available, partly because the data, methods, and code are publicly available. The downscaled projections have been accessed on the host NASA and AWS servers millions of times, and NEX-GDDP was among the most-requested datasets by Google Earth Engine users before it was added to their public data holdings in 2023. NEX-GDDP has had wide-reaching impact in academia, government, and the private sector. The projections have been used in more than 700 peer-reviewed journal articles examining climate change impacts, temperature and heat events, precipitation, hydrology, agriculture and food security, extreme events and disasters, regional climate studies, environmental and ecological impacts, and human health and socio-economic impacts. Forty of these papers can be found in the…"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "Dataset",
      "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:dataset:agu-0087",
      "mainEntityOfPage": "https://impactfuldatasets.agu.org/#/dataset/agu-0087",
      "identifier": [
        {
          "@type": "PropertyValue",
          "propertyID": "AGU-Impactful-Datasets-ID",
          "value": "agu-0087"
        }
      ],
      "name": "National Energy Water Treatment and Speciation (NEWTS) Database",
      "alternateName": "",
      "keywords": {
        "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:theme:ocean"
      },
      "agu:datasetId": "agu-0087",
      "agu:stableKey": "title:national energy water treatment and speciation (newts) database",
      "agu:nominatorCount": 1,
      "agu:citationCount": 1,
      "agu:reuseCount": 5,
      "description": "The NEWTS database serves as a centralized digital resource offering cleaned, standardized, and reformatted geochemical data essential for evaluating fossil energy wastewater treatment, beneficial reuse strategies, and critical minerals recovery. This resource significantly enhances the accessibility and usability of fossil energy wastewater chemistry data. Hosted on NETL's Energy Data eXchange (EDX), the NEWTS group comprises 171 individual resources, including tabular geochemical datasets from over 400,000 wastewater samples, chemical modeling software templates and input files for OLI Studio and Geochemist's Workbench (GWB), geospatial data, and case studies. Additionally, it provides data-based tools such as the NEWTS Federal Database Dashboard, the NEWTS State-Level Database Dashboard, and the Constituent Data Replacement Tool (CoDaRT) for imputing missing constituent data, along with video tutorials to guide users.",
      "url": "https://edx.netl.doe.gov/group/newts",
      "creator": [
        {
          "@type": "Person",
          "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:person:rachel-yesenchak-devin-justman-lucy-romeo-isabelle-pfander-justin-mack",
          "name": "Rachel Yesenchak, Devin Justman, Lucy Romeo, Isabelle Pfander, Justin Mackey, Sophia Bauer, Michael Sabbatino, Burt Thomas, Zineb Belarbi, Madison Wenzlick, Kathryn Smith, Chad Able, Alison Fritz, Nicholas Siefert"
        }
      ],
      "agu:curator": [
        {
          "@type": "Person",
          "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:person:national-energy-technology-laboratory-netl",
          "name": "National Energy Technology Laboratory (NETL)"
        }
      ],
      "includedInDataCatalog": {
        "@type": "DataCatalog",
        "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:organization:energy-data-exchange-edx",
        "name": "Energy Data eXchange (EDX)"
      },
      "citation": [
        {
          "@type": "CreativeWork",
          "text": "Smith, K., Z. Belarbi, I. Pfander, R. Yesenchak, J. Mackey, L. Romeo, D. Justman, M. Wenzlick, R. Thomas, H. Hadjeres, C. Able, A. Fritz, N. Siefert. (2025). National Energy Water Treatment and Speciation (NEWTS) Database and Dashboards: New Resources for Locating and Assessing Energy-Related…"
        }
      ],
      "agu:reuseExample": [
        {
          "@type": "CreativeWork",
          "text": "These data have been applied to develop average compositions to inform process models for treatment of energy wastewaters. An example of this use case is shown in the table below:"
        },
        {
          "@type": "CreativeWork",
          "text": "Able, C., Schmitt, T., Siefert, N., & Fritz, A. (2025). Baseline cost analysis of energy wastewater treatment with preliminary feasibility analysis of critical mineral recovery. Minerals, 15(3), 213.…"
        },
        {
          "@type": "CreativeWork",
          "text": "The database was also used in the following manuscript to complete a resource assessment of critical minerals in produced water:"
        },
        {
          "@type": "CreativeWork",
          "text": "Smith, K. H., Mackey, J. E., Wenzlick, M., Thomas, B., & Siefert, N. S. (2024). Critical mineral source potential from oil & gas produced waters in the United States. Science of The Total…"
        },
        {
          "@type": "CreativeWork",
          "text": "Finally, these data have been applied for development of synthetic compositions of energy wastewaters that are used in experiments for treatment and mineral recovery technologies."
        }
      ],
      "agu:nominator": [
        {
          "@type": "Person",
          "@id": "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7470-6602",
          "name": "Alison Fritz",
          "affiliation": {
            "@type": "Organization",
            "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:organization:national-energy-technology-laboratory",
            "name": "National Energy Technology Laboratory"
          },
          "agu:sequence": 1
        }
      ],
      "agu:justification": [
        {
          "@type": "CreativeWork",
          "agu:sequence": 1,
          "text": "The NEWTS database was nominated because it addresses critical challenges in managing energy wastewater, fostering advancements across multiple dimensions. NEWTS significantly enhances educational and training opportunities by providing a readily accessible, standardized dataset for researchers and students. This facilitates deeper understanding of wastewater characteristics and treatment processes, specifically giving student researchers an opportunity to understand realistic energy wastewater parameters without conducting time and resource limited data collection. By consolidating and standardizing diverse energy water stream data, NEWTS also enables more accurate assessment of geophysical phenomena related to water contamination and resource availability. It supports conservation efforts by facilitating the design of effective treatment and reuse strategies, reducing environmental…"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "Dataset",
      "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:dataset:agu-0088",
