        }
      ],
      "agu:reuseExample": [
        {
          "@type": "CreativeWork",
          "text": "Sohl, T., Jin, S., Dewitz, J., Wickham, J., Brown, J., Stehman, S., Herold, N., Schleeweis, K., Tollerud, H., & Deering, C. (2025). Thirty years of the u. S. National land cover database: Impacts and…"
        },
        {
          "@type": "CreativeWork",
          "text": "There are over 10,000 cited uses of NLCD. There's a table in the above paper that notes cited uses of NLCD for many different sectors. That table is provided here in list form, with major sectors (no…"
        },
        {
          "@type": "CreativeWork",
          "text": "Energy Development Biofuel development Stoof et al. 2015; Baxter and Calvert 2017; Austin et al. 2022 Wind development and siting Kiesecker et al. 2011; Fargione et al. 2012; Dai and Scown 2025…"
        },
        {
          "@type": "CreativeWork",
          "text": "Human Health Mosquitoes and disease risk Bowden et al. 2011; Wiese et al. 2019; Bondo et al. 2022 Lyme disease risk Diuk-Wasser et al. 2012; Ballard and Bone 2021 COVID incidence You and Pan 2020;…"
        },
        {
          "@type": "CreativeWork",
          "text": "Natural Hazards Flooding vulnerability (inland) Qiang et al. 2017; Tate et al. 2021; Banjara et al. 2024 Coastal storm surge Bunya et al. 2010; Haddad et al. 2015; Yarveysi et al. 2025 Landslide…"
        }
      ],
      "agu:nominator": [
        {
          "@type": "Person",
          "@id": "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9771-4231",
          "name": "Terry Sohl",
          "affiliation": {
            "@type": "Organization",
            "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:organization:us-geological-survey-earth-resources-observation-and-science-eros-cent",
            "name": "US Geological Survey, Earth Resources Observation and Science (EROS) Center, 47914 252nd Street, Sioux Falls, South Dakota 57104"
          },
          "agu:sequence": 1
        }
      ],
      "agu:justification": [
        {
          "@type": "CreativeWork",
          "agu:sequence": 1,
          "text": "The National Land Cover Database (NLCD) was initiated 30 years ago and has continually provided critical land-cover and land-change information for the United States. Originally launched to address the lack of national-scale, moderate-resolution land-cover data, NLCD has evolved from the pioneering 1992 dataset into the latest release, Annual NLCD 1985-2024, providing annual land cover, land cover change, forest canopy, impervious surface, and other land-change variables. A new, innovative AI-based methodology was developed, linking 3 deep learning models to simultaneously produce land cover and impervious surface variables, greatly reducing product latency, consistency, and accuracy. Throughout its history, NLCD has become an essential resource for scientific research, land management, and policy development. Over 10,300 scientific publications cite NLCD, including over 9,300…"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "Dataset",
      "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:dataset:agu-0089",
      "mainEntityOfPage": "https://impactfuldatasets.agu.org/#/dataset/agu-0089",
      "identifier": [
        {
          "@type": "PropertyValue",
