      "agu:justification": [
        {
          "@type": "CreativeWork",
          "agu:sequence": 1,
          "text": "PARMA/EXPACS was nominated because the dataset turns atmospheric cosmic-ray radiation from a specialist topic into shared, auditable infrastructure. Before PARMA, realistic atmospheric fluxes were practical only for experts with large compute resources and Monte Carlo skills. By packaging rigorous physics in an easy-to-use tool, PARMA/EXPACS democratized access and broadened applications well beyond radiation and space physics. PEOPLE Aircrew dose rises with altitude; accordingly, flight crews—like ground-based radiation workers—require appropriate monitoring and management. In Japan, tools built on PARMA, such as JISCARD (http://www.jiscard.jp/) (in Japanese) and WASAVIES (https://wasavies.nict.go.jp/index_e.html), are used by airlines to estimate route- and fleet-specific exposures and to maintain crew dose records [1-7]. Beyond aviation, PARMA provides transparent, location- and…"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "Dataset",
      "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:dataset:agu-0103",
