      "name": "SatPM2.5 (Satellite-derived PM2.5) with current versions: V6.GL.02.04 (global, 1998–2023, Convolutional Neural Network based calibration), V5.GL.05.02 (global, 1998–2023, Geographically Weighted Regression based calibration), and V5.NA.05/V5.NA.05.02 (North American, 2000–2023, compositional PM2.5)",
      "alternateName": "",
      "keywords": {
        "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:theme:atmos"
      },
      "agu:datasetId": "agu-0106",
      "agu:stableKey": "title:satpm2.5 (satellite-derived pm2.5) with current versions: v6.gl.02.04 (global, 1998–2023, convolutional neural network based calibration), v5.gl.05.02 (global, 1998–2023, geographically weighted regression based calibration), and v5.na.05/v5.na.05.02 (north american, 2000–2023, compositional pm2.5)",
      "agu:nominatorCount": 1,
      "agu:citationCount": 3,
      "agu:reuseCount": 12,
      "description": "SatPM2.5 is a collection of datasets providing spatially and temporally continuous global and regional estimates of ground-level fine particulate matter (PM2.5). The datasets combine Aerosol Optical Depth (AOD) retrievals from multiple satellite-based instruments (MODIS/Terra, MODIS/Aqua, MISR/Terra, SeaWiFS/SeaStar, VIIRS/SNPP, and VIIRS/NOAA20), with chemical transport model simulations (GEOS-Chem) and ground-based observations. The current data collection includes several scientific versions: V6.GL.02.04 (global, 1998–2023, Convolutional Neural Network based calibration), V5.GL.05.02 (global, 1998–2023, Geographically Weighted Regression based calibration), and V5.NA.05/V5.NA.05.02 (North American, 2000–2023, compositional PM2.5). The datasets are provided at both high spatial resolution (0.01° × 0.01°) and reduced resolution (0.1° × 0.1°), with annual, monthly, and biweekly time-scales. For ease of accessibility, SatPM2.5 includes several processed datasets, including population-weighted estimates derived from the V5.GL.05.02 and V6.GL.02.04 scientific versions. Adapted from…",
      "url": "https://satpm.org/",
