      "agu:justification": [
        {
          "@type": "CreativeWork",
          "agu:sequence": 1,
          "text": "SatPM2.5 is an impactful dataset providing accessible data for researchers, policymakers, and communities to better understand global and regional PM2.5 exposure. The data enable analyses that support decision-making and policy, filling in gaps where ground-based monitors are sparse or absent. The data are relied upon by a large and growing health and air quality management community including the American Lung Association (ALA), Air Quality Life Index, Environmental Performance Index, EPA, Global Burden of Disease, HEI State of Global Air, OECD, NOAA, UNDP, WHO, World Bank, UNICEF, US Census Bureau, air quality managers and forecasters, private companies, non-governmental organizations, numerous environmental health scientists, and the general public. These data have thus contributed to the growing awareness of the health and environmental effects of ambient PM2.5. A specific example…"
        }
      ]
    },
