      "name": "Sea Ice Index",
      "alternateName": "",
      "keywords": {
        "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:theme:ocean"
      },
      "agu:datasetId": "agu-0107",
      "agu:stableKey": "doi:10.7265/a98x-0f50|sea ice index",
      "agu:nominatorCount": 1,
      "agu:citationCount": 3,
      "agu:reuseCount": 5,
      "description": "The Sea Ice Index provides sea ice extent and area data for both hemispheres, using satellite passive microwave-derived sea ice concentration fields as input. The simple, quick-to-understand and up-to-date graphs and maps have contributed to growing awareness of how rapidly the Earth, particularly the Arctic, is changing. It is a source for ice extent and concentration images and data values from November 1978 to the present. Sea Ice Index images also depict trends and anomalies in ice cover calculated using a 30-year reference period of 1981 through 2010. The images and data are produced in a consistent way that makes the Index timeseries appropriate for use when looking at long-term trends in sea ice cover. (From the Overview on the product landing page, https://nsidc.org/data/g02135/versions/4 ) The Sea Ice Index was first published in 2002. It was envisioned as a website that would meet a need for readily accessible, easy-to-use information on sea ice trends and anomalies, with products that would assist in monitoring and diagnosing the ice extent minima that were gaining…",
      "url": "https://doi.org/10.7265/a98x-0f50",
