      "agu:justification": [
        {
          "@type": "CreativeWork",
          "agu:sequence": 2,
          "text": "The NSIDC Sea Ice Index (SII) exemplifies the meaning of an “impactful dataset,” with influence spanning science, policy, and education. One of the most visible indicators of human-caused climate change is Arctic sea-ice loss, and the SII has become the standard for translating the satellite-derived sea ice record into a trusted data product for monitoring changes across both polar regions. The SII underpins original scientific research, supports real-time ice monitoring for shipping and other socioeconomic sectors, and serves as a foundation for science communication while also informing legislators on adaptation planning. A central strength of the SII is its deliberate design to be both rigorous and broadly accessible, with well-maintained formats, clear documentation, and extensive resources that enable nonexperts to engage with the data. It has also become a go-to dataset for…"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "Dataset",
      "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:dataset:agu-0108",
