      "name": "Sofar Spotter Data Archive",
      "alternateName": "",
      "keywords": {
        "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:theme:ocean"
      },
      "agu:datasetId": "agu-0108",
      "agu:stableKey": "title:sofar spotter data archive",
      "agu:nominatorCount": 1,
      "agu:citationCount": 1,
      "agu:reuseCount": 1,
      "description": "The Sofar Spotter Data Archive is a globally distributed, open-access collection of ocean wave, wind, and temperature observations gathered by Sofar’s Spotter buoys — a network of low-cost, solar-powered ocean sensors. The archive aggregates years of continuous measurements from thousands of locations across the world’s oceans, spanning coastal and open-ocean environments. This dataset provides an unprecedented view of surface ocean dynamics, enabling research in air-sea interaction, climate variability, extreme wave prediction, and coastal resilience. By openly sharing these data through GitHub, Sofar Ocean aims to accelerate scientific discovery, foster reproducible oceanography, and support equitable access to ocean data for scientists, policymakers, and educators worldwide.",
      "url": "https://github.com/sofarocean/spotter-data-archive",
      "creator": [
        {
          "@type": "Person",
          "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:person:isabel-houghton",
          "name": "Isabel Houghton"
        },
        {
          "@type": "Person",
          "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:person:pieter-smit",
          "name": "Pieter Smit"
        },
        {
          "@type": "Person",
          "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:person:ciara-dorsay",
          "name": "Ciara Dorsay"
        }
      ],
      "agu:curator": [
        {
          "@type": "Person",
          "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:person:sofar-ocean-open-data-team",
          "name": "Sofar Ocean Open Data Team"
        }
      ],
      "includedInDataCatalog": {
        "@type": "DataCatalog",
        "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:organization:sofar-spotter-archive",
        "name": "sofar-spotter-archive"
      },
      "citation": [
        {
          "@type": "CreativeWork",
          "text": "Houghton, I. A., Smit, P. B., Clark, D., Dunning, C., Fisher, A., Nidzieko, N. J., Chamberlain, P., & Janssen, T. T. (2021). Performance statistics of a real-time pacific ocean weather sensor network. Journal of Atmospheric and Oceanic Technology, 38(5), 1047–1058.…"
        }
      ],
      "agu:reuseExample": [
        {
          "@type": "CreativeWork",
          "text": "Eldrett JS, Ma C, Bergman S, Lutz B, Gregory FJ, Dodsworth P, Phipps M, Hardas P, Minisini D, Ozkan A, Ramezani J, Bowring SA, Kamo SL, Ferguson K, Macaulay C, Kelly AE. 2015a. An astronomically…"
        }
      ],
      "agu:nominator": [
        {
          "@type": "Person",
          "@id": "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-1288-8636",
          "name": "Anna Savage",
          "affiliation": {
            "@type": "Organization",
            "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:organization:sofar-ocean-pier-28-annex-san-francisco-ca-94105-usa",
            "name": "Sofar Ocean, Pier 28 Annex, San Francisco, CA 94105, USA"
          },
          "agu:sequence": 1
        }
      ],
      "agu:justification": [
        {
          "@type": "CreativeWork",
          "agu:sequence": 1,
          "text": "The Sofar Spotter Data Archive exemplifies an impactful dataset across all three AGU impact dimensions — People, Planet, and Prosperity. People: This dataset democratizes access to high-quality ocean observations. By removing financial and logistical barriers to ocean monitoring, it supports training, education, and global research collaboration. The data have been used in university labs, graduate theses, and by government agencies. The open-source analysis examples and tutorials available on GitHub further enhance its educational impact, providing hands-on training in data processing, spectral analysis, and oceanographic interpretation using real-world datasets. Planet: The archive contributes directly to our understanding of ocean-climate interactions and environmental change. With wave and wind data from both under-observed and remote ocean regions, researchers can use these…",
          "agu:impactDimension": [
            {
              "@type": "DefinedTerm",
              "name": "People",
              "description": "This dataset democratizes access to high-quality ocean observations. By removing financial and logistical barriers to ocean monitoring, it supports training, education, and global research collaboration. The data have been used in university labs, graduate theses, and by government agencies. The open-source analysis examples and tutorials available on GitHub further enhance its educational impact, providing hands-on…"
            },
            {
              "@type": "DefinedTerm",
              "name": "Planet",
              "description": "The archive contributes directly to our understanding of ocean-climate interactions and environmental change. With wave and wind data from both under-observed and remote ocean regions, researchers can use these observations to validate global wave models, monitor marine heatwaves, and study tropical cyclones. The global coverage and consistency of this dataset make it uniquely suited for climate monitoring and model…"
            },
            {
              "@type": "DefinedTerm",
              "name": "Prosperity",
              "description": "By underpinning applications in renewable energy siting, coastal infrastructure design, and navigation safety, this dataset can contribute to economic and community resilience. The open-access model also supports equitable participation in the blue economy — from startups to nations — ensuring that environmental intelligence benefits all. Without the Spotter Data Archive, the ocean science community would lack one…"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "Dataset",
      "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:dataset:agu-0109",
      "mainEntityOfPage": "https://impactfuldatasets.agu.org/#/dataset/agu-0109",
      "identifier": [
        {
          "@type": "PropertyValue",
          "propertyID": "AGU-Impactful-Datasets-ID",
          "value": "agu-0109"
        }
      ],
      "name": "Soil Respiration Database",
      "alternateName": "",
      "keywords": {
        "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:theme:biosphere"
      },
      "agu:datasetId": "agu-0109",
      "agu:stableKey": "title:soil respiration database",
      "agu:nominatorCount": 1,
      "agu:citationCount": 1,
      "agu:reuseCount": 1,
      "description": "The Soil Respiration Database (SRDB) is a near-universal compendium of published soil respiration (Rs) data. The database encompasses published studies that report at least one of the following data measured in the field (not laboratory): annual soil respiration, mean seasonal soil respiration, a seasonal or annual partitioning of soil respiration into its source fluxes, soil respiration temperature response (Q10), or soil respiration at 10 degrees C. The SRDB's orientation is to seasonal and annual fluxes, not shorter-term or chamber-specific measurements, and the database is dominated by temperate, well-drained forest measurement locations.",
      "url": "https://d3o6w55j8uz1ro.cloudfront.net/s3-d0f68fa49c8cba12794bb586349f2341/ornl-cumulus-prod-public.s3.us-west-2.amazonaws.com/global_soil/SRDB_V5/comp/SRDB_V5.pdf?A-userid=None&Expires=1757104741&Signature=BY3TpZNLMBBak3ao3-ZF2ggdP2NZwLJma5BneSJWZ21mmISF8Lh~SIlPV-9q2As-62u4ropmKctoTE~5IQs0Rtu-zGixAbiKh9OxONbe5KHgC5T~6DYzUhLN2G2Le5ysRREUBBwrYTrjOLl~pLLS3RDsS5xMhiIxJgWbxl2MPqVivI9FT8mH6ORSHCOr803YLhDoT99V2l7XtCR3hemgFkc1SxU7-5hOdA1hO5BqAlvaiIUfFpo2aeHl0lrAvwmlZlwgA2mQReyf-Hv6BJBACag1~JgHHHKpbg2h4jeb~5dlxNUtAV5eYEdnkSyB44t9Qlhc1cSX9cuTs1auJ7qLEg__&Key-Pair-Id=K3C82G6IBNME9J",
      "creator": [
        {
          "@type": "Person",
          "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:person:ben-bond-lamberty",
          "name": "Ben Bond-Lamberty"
        }
      ],
      "includedInDataCatalog": {
        "@type": "DataCatalog",
        "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:organization:ornl-daac",
        "name": "ORNL DAAC"
      },
      "citation": [
        {
          "@type": "CreativeWork",
          "text": "Jian, J., Vargas, R., Anderson-Teixeira, K., Stell, E., Herrmann, V., Horn, M., Kholod, N., Manzon, J., Marchesi, R., Paredes, D., & Bond-Lamberty, B. (2021). A restructured and updated global soil respiration database (Srdb-v5). Earth System Science Data, 13(2), 255–267.…"
        }
      ],
      "agu:reuseExample": [
        {
          "@type": "CreativeWork",
          "text": "Bond-Lamberty, B., Bailey, V. L., Chen, M., Gough, C. M., & Vargas, R. (2018). Globally rising soil heterotrophic respiration over recent decades. Nature, 560(7716), 80–83.…"
        }
      ],
      "agu:nominator": [
        {
          "@type": "Person",
          "@id": "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7850-6402",
          "name": "Avni Malhotra",
          "affiliation": {
            "@type": "Organization",
            "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:organization:biological-sciences-division-pacific-northwest-national-laboratory-902",
            "name": "Biological Sciences Division, Pacific Northwest National Laboratory, 902 Battelle Boulevard, Richland, WA 99354"
          },
          "agu:sequence": 1
        }
      ],
      "agu:justification": [
        {
          "@type": "CreativeWork",
          "agu:sequence": 1,
          "text": "This database pioneered the synthesis of chamber-based measurements of CO2 released from soils globally. Prior to this database, chamber data were present for individual sites, in different formats and unusable for synthesis or modeling questions. Since its release, the community has been able to answer various questions about the controls on soil respiration, changes over time, and gaps in our understanding. The database has generated various high impact papers, revealing phenomena about the soil respiration that were previously unknown. This database has also enabled the training of over half a dozen high school interns, graduate students, and postdocs on database development, programming, ecosystem science, etc."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "Dataset",
      "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:dataset:agu-0110",
      "mainEntityOfPage": "https://impactfuldatasets.agu.org/#/dataset/agu-0110",
      "identifier": [
        {
          "@type": "PropertyValue",
          "propertyID": "AGU-Impactful-Datasets-ID",
          "value": "agu-0110"
        },
        {
          "@type": "PropertyValue",
          "propertyID": "DOI",
          "value": "https://doi.org/10.5287/ora-2nanwp4rk"
        }
      ],
      "name": "Speleothem Isotope Synthesis and AnaLysis v1, v1b, v2, v3",
      "alternateName": "",
      "keywords": {
        "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:theme:biosphere"
      },
      "agu:datasetId": "agu-0110",
      "agu:stableKey": "doi:10.5287/ora-2nanwp4rk|speleothem isotope synthesis and analysis v1, v1b, v2, v3",
      "agu:nominatorCount": 1,
      "agu:citationCount": 1,
      "agu:reuseCount": 1,
      "description": "Stable isotope and trace elements records from speleothems provide information on past climate changes, most particularly information that can be used to reconstruct past changes in precipitation and atmospheric circulation. SISAL (Speleothem Isotope Synthesis and Analysis) is an international working group of the Past Global Changes (PAGES) project. The working group aims to provide a comprehensive compilation of speleothem isotope and trace elements records for climate reconstruction and model evaluation. SISALv3 database contains 892 oxygen isotope, 620 carbon isotope, 95 Mg/Ca, 85 Sr/Ca, 52 Ba/Ca, 25 U/Ca, 29 P/Ca and 14 Sr isotope records from 838 speleothems from 365 cave sites worldwide, and metadata describing the cave settings and age models of these records. This version contains standardized age-depth models. There are also 51 datafiles containing trace element data and 246 image files of cave maps and entity scans. https://ora.ox.ac.uk/objects/uuid:1e91e2ac-ca9f-46e5-85f3-8d82d4d3cfd4",
      "url": "https://doi.org/10.5287/ora-2nanwp4rk",
      "creator": [
        {
          "@type": "Person",
          "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:person:kamolphat-atsawawaranunt",
          "name": "Kamolphat Atsawawaranunt"
        },
        {
          "@type": "Person",
          "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:person:laia-comas-bru",
          "name": "Laia COmas-Bru"
        },
        {
          "@type": "Person",
          "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:person:nikita-kaushal",
          "name": "Nikita Kaushal"
        },
        {
          "@type": "Person",
          "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:person:franziska-lechleitner",
          "name": "Franziska Lechleitner"
        }
      ],
      "agu:curator": [
        {
          "@type": "Person",
          "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:person:pages-sisal-working-group",
          "name": "PAGES SISAL Working Group"
        }
      ],
      "includedInDataCatalog": {
        "@type": "DataCatalog",
        "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:organization:ncei-noaa-and-oxford-university-research-archive",
        "name": "NCEI NOAA and Oxford University Research Archive"
      },
      "citation": [
        {
          "@type": "CreativeWork",
          "text": "https://essd.copernicus.org/articles/16/1933/2024/essd-16-1933-2024.pdf"
        }
      ],
      "agu:reuseExample": [
        {
          "@type": "CreativeWork",
          "text": "https://pastglobalchanges.org/science/wg/sisal/publications"
        }
      ],
      "agu:nominator": [
        {
          "@type": "Person",
          "@id": "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2220-9046",
          "name": "Nikita Kaushal",
          "affiliation": {
            "@type": "Organization",
            "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:organization:american-museum-of-natural-history-200-central-park-west-new-york-ny-1",
            "name": "American Museum of Natural History, 200 Central Park West, New York, NY 10024, USA"
          },
          "agu:sequence": 1
        }
      ],
      "agu:justification": [
        {
          "@type": "CreativeWork",
          "agu:sequence": 1,
          "text": "People: education - the data are great for training paleoclimate researchers on time series analysis given the standardised age depth models that have been made available with the dataset. The dataset has been made available on the SISAL WebApp (https://geochem.hu/SISAL_webApp/). The WebApp provides SQL code together with data download queries to train researchers on using SQL. Planet: climate - speleothems provide oxygen isotope data for reconstructing large scale circulation and hydroclimatic changes with absolute chronologies going back 500,000 years. They also provide critical data for climate model benchmarking particularly of water isotope enabeled models.",
          "agu:impactDimension": [
            {
              "@type": "DefinedTerm",
              "name": "People",
              "description": "education - the data are great for training paleoclimate researchers on time series analysis given the standardised age depth models that have been made available with the dataset. The dataset has been made available on the SISAL WebApp (https://geochem.hu/SISAL_webApp/). The WebApp provides SQL code together with data download queries to train researchers on using SQL."
            },
            {
              "@type": "DefinedTerm",
              "name": "Planet",
              "description": "climate - speleothems provide oxygen isotope data for reconstructing large scale circulation and hydroclimatic changes with absolute chronologies going back 500,000 years. They also provide critical data for climate model benchmarking particularly of water isotope enabeled models."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "Dataset",
      "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:dataset:agu-0111",
      "mainEntityOfPage": "https://impactfuldatasets.agu.org/#/dataset/agu-0111",
      "identifier": [
        {
          "@type": "PropertyValue",
          "propertyID": "AGU-Impactful-Datasets-ID",
          "value": "agu-0111"
        },
        {
          "@type": "PropertyValue",
          "propertyID": "DOI",
          "value": "https://doi.org/10.4211/hs.92577b67675d4695b37f27a3b79ded85"
        }
      ],
      "name": "Stable isotope tempestology database",
      "alternateName": "",
      "keywords": {
        "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:theme:surface"
      },
      "agu:datasetId": "agu-0111",
      "agu:stableKey": "doi:10.4211/hs.92577b67675d4695b37f27a3b79ded85|stable isotope tempestology database",
      "agu:nominatorCount": 1,
      "agu:citationCount": 1,
      "agu:reuseCount": 3,
      "description": "This database documents the isotopic characteristics of 40 tropical cyclones (ranging from tropical depressions/storms to Category 5 hurricanes), including recent (2012-2023) and archived (1984-1995) observations. This database is part of the isotope tempestology collaborative research network (2016-present) (known as STORM; https://tropicalwaterscr.wixsite.com/hydro/storm) across the North Atlantic and Eastern Pacific Ocean basins. This initiative has been centered mainly on collecting and analyzing recent high-frequency (hourly to daily) samples of precipitation (P), surface water (SW), and groundwater (GW) during TC landfalls and passages to improve the understanding of isotope tempestology processes.",
      "url": "https://doi.org/10.4211/hs.92577b67675d4695b37f27a3b79ded85",
      "creator": [
        {
          "@type": "Person",
          "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:person:ricardo-sanchez-murillo",
          "name": "Ricardo Sanchez-Murillo"
        }
      ],
      "agu:curator": [
        {
          "@type": "Person",
          "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:person:cuahsi",
          "name": "CUAHSI"
        }
