          "@type": "CreativeWork",
          "text": "Boving, I., Allen, J., Brodrick, P. G., Chadwick, K. D., Trugman, A., & Anderegg, L. D. L. (2025). The unstable relationship between drought status and leaf water content complicates the remote…"
        }
      ],
      "agu:nominator": [
        {
          "@type": "Person",
          "@id": "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5633-4865",
          "name": "K. Dana Chadwick",
          "affiliation": {
            "@type": "Organization",
            "@id": "urn:org:agu:data:impactful-datasets:id:organization:nasa-jet-propulsion-laboratory-california-institute-of-technology-4800",
            "name": "NASA Jet Propulsion Laboratory, California Institute of Technology, 4800 Oak Grove Dr, Pasadena, CA 91109"
          },
          "agu:sequence": 1
        }
      ],
      "agu:justification": [
        {
          "@type": "CreativeWork",
          "agu:sequence": 1,
          "text": "The Surface Biology and Geology (SBG) High-Frequency Time Series (SHIFT) dataset was nominated because it represents a pivotal advance in Earth observation science, capturing the first-ever dense sub-seasonal hyperspectral record of terrestrial and aquatic ecosystems. Without SHIFT, the empirical foundation needed to understand how biological and biophysical processes evolve at the critical timescales—days to weeks—when ecosystems respond to stress, disturbance, and climate variability would be lacking. People – Education, Training, and Disaster Readiness SHIFT stands out as a model for open, inclusive, and capacity-building science. From its inception, the campaign prioritized participation by early career researchers, graduate and undergraduate students, and postdoctoral scholars. More than 40 emerging scientists from universities and research organizations were trained in…"
        }
      ]
    },
