      "agu:justification": [
        {
          "@type": "CreativeWork",
          "agu:sequence": 1,
          "text": "The World Wide Lightning Location Network (WWLLN) dataset is one of the most influential and widely utilized global lightning datasets in atmospheric and geophysical research. Since its establishment, WWLLN has enabled continuous, near real-time monitoring of global lightning activity and has supported a broad spectrum of studies spanning atmospheric electricity, severe weather, tropical cyclones, climate variability, ionospheric disturbances, upper atmospheric phenomena, wildfire detection, and space weather applications. The scientific impact of the WWLLN dataset is substantial and continues to grow. To date, more than 3,500 peer-reviewed research articles have been published using WWLLN data, demonstrating its extensive adoption across the international research community. In addition, the dataset has contributed to over 40 doctoral and graduate theses worldwide, reflecting its…"
        }
      ]
    },
