      "agu:citationCount": 4,
      "agu:reuseCount": 8,
      "description": "The ESA WorldCereal consortium has built a global, community-based and open repository of harmonized reference data on land cover, crop type and irrigation information. Currently covering more than150 datasets across the globe, these data are typically used to construct and validate global to regional high-resolution cropland and crop type maps. We define reference data as all data which can either be used for calibrating classification algorithms or validating the resulting products. As such, reference data should contain location- and time-specific information about land cover and/or crop type. Examples include in-situ field observations gathered through dedicated field surveys, farmers declarations through parcel registration systems, observations derived from visual or automated interpretation of very high-resolution satellite imagery or in-situ photographs, or existing high-quality classified maps based on analysis of satellite imagery. Reference data is typically available in different formats depending on the source of the dataset. To ensure multiple datasets can be…",
      "url": "https://zenodo.org/records/18769612",
      "creator": [
